% Bugs in a C program that the pointer analysis can show, whatever the
% order of its statements (docs/plans/plan_dotnet_languages.md, the
% end goal): run with pointer.dl, over mini-cc's facts (Facts.mli) and
% three relations that mini-analyze says of the places:
%   heap(L)        L is what an allocator gave ('_malloc_in_f_line_N')
%   local(L, F)    L is F's own, its frame's (a local or a parameter
%                  whose address is taken, a local array's elements)
%   literal(L)     L is a string written in the program
%   bad_free(I, L)   the call I of free may be given L, not the heap's
%   dangling(F, L)   F may return the address of its own local L
%   unset_call(I)    the call I through a pointer reaches nothing: a
%                    pointer no function is put in (null, most often)
% Each may be wrong where the analysis is coarse (a pointer that may
% point to two places is said to point to both), never because of
% the order: so "may".
%
% design:
% The checks are the analysis's answers read with one more fact each:
% a place is the heap's, a frame's or a string's, which the facts'
% names already say and mini-analyze makes relations of. Nothing here
% knows the order of statements: free(p); p = malloc(n); is no bug
% here and use after free is not found; that needs the order (a flow-
% sensitive analysis, its facts per program point, liveness.dl's kind)
% or the shapes of the heap (separation logic: Infer's).
%
% others:
% Dawson Engler's checkers (Stanford, 2000; then Coverity) wrote
% rules of a system's code (a lock taken is released, a freed pointer
% not used) as small automata run over each path, and found thousands
% of bugs in Linux; Saturn (Yichen Xie, Alex Aiken, 2005) the same
% checks by a SAT solver, function by function with summaries; Infer
% (Facebook, 2015, from Cristiano Calcagno, Dino Distefano, Peter
% O'Hearn's separation logic) memory bugs proved absent or found, one
% function at a time, on every commit; CodeQL (Semmle, Oege de Moor,
% from 2007) queries of a program's database, in a Datalog with
% classes. Here the checks are three rules over Andersen's answers.
%
% References: Dawson Engler, Benjamin Chelf, Andy Chou, Seth Hallem,
% "Checking system rules using system-specific, programmer-written
% compiler extensions" (OSDI 2000); Yichen Xie, Alex Aiken, "Saturn:
% A scalable framework for error detection using Boolean
% satisfiability" (TOPLAS 2007); Cristiano Calcagno and others,
% "Moving fast with software verification" (NFM 2015).

freed(I, L) :- call_direct(I, free), argument(I, 1, V), point_to(V, L).
bad_free(I, L) :- freed(I, L), \+ heap(L).

dangling(F, L) :- return(F, R), point_to(R, L), local(L, F).

reaches(I) :- call_edge(I, F).
unset_call(I) :- call_indirect(I, V), \+ reaches(I).
